CImg Library
Project manager: David Tschumperlé
https://cimg.eu/

CImg is bundled inside Matplot++
(extern/matplotplusplus/source/3rd_party/cimg/CImg.h) and is compiled into
libmatplot.

CImg is dual-licensed: the recipient may choose EITHER

  * the CeCILL-C license (a weak, file-level copyleft, close to the GNU LGPL), OR
  * the CeCILL v2.1 license (a strong copyleft, compatible with the GNU GPL).

For the HOPS distribution we elect the **CeCILL-C** license (the LGPL-like
arm), under which CImg may be incorporated as a component into a larger work
distributed under other terms here, the MIT-licensed HOPS. We do NOT elect the
CeCILL / CeCILL v2.1 arm.

The full text of the CeCILL-C Free Software License Agreement, version 1, is
provided alongside this file as Licence_CeCILL-C_V1-en.txt, and is also
published at:

    https://cecill.info/licences/Licence_CeCILL-C_V1-en.txt

The governing license notice as distributed by the CImg authors is retained
verbatim in the bundled CImg.h source file.
